data.judge_completion:
The reflection matrix $ R $ is determined by the given transformation. Since the reflection matrix $ R $ satisfies $ R \vec{v} = \vec{w} $, and we know that the original vector $ \vec{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} $ maps to $ \vec{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} $, we can find the matrix $ R $.

By solving the system of equations derived from $ R \vec{v} = \vec{w} $, we find:

$$
R = \begin{pmatrix}
\frac{4}{5} & \frac{3}{5} \\
\frac{3}{5} & -\frac{4}{5}
\end{pmatrix}
$$

To find the image of $ \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} $, we apply the matrix:

$$
R \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix}
\frac{4}{5} \cdot (-2) + \frac{3}{5} \cdot 3 \\
\frac{3}{5} \cdot (-2) + \left(-\frac{4}{5}\right) \cdot 3
\end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix}
\frac{1}{5} \\
-\frac{18}{5}
\end{pmatrix}
$$

Thus, the reflection takes $ \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} $ to $ \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{5} \\ -\frac{18}{5} \end{pmatrix}} $.

